# Built-in application classification for ActivityOS.
#
# One rule per line:  category | flags | match | application name
# Rules are read top to bottom and the first one that matches wins. An
# application that matches nothing is "Other". User rules from Settings are
# applied afterwards and override these.
#
# flags   -            none
#         distraction  time in this application counts as a potential distraction
#         browser      classify by the active tab's URL or title when available
#
# match   exact  the whole name equals the text. Use this for short or ordinary
#                words ("arc", "nova"), where a longer name is a different app.
#         words  the text appears in the name as whole, consecutive words:
#                "visual studio" matches "Visual Studio Code".
#
# Names are compared in lowercase with a trailing ".exe" removed, and words are
# split on anything that is not a letter or digit ("sublime_text" is two words).

